    "related_formalizations": [
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/stalex444/werner-window/tree/81c70fe45f81da86c25254f3eb52123d504b452c",
        "note": "Palomar PALOMAR-2026-09-01-000003. Among other results it proves that every separable density matrix has CHSH expectation at most 2 at arbitrary finite local dimensions and Hermitian-involution settings (EntangledBorn.separable_chsh_le_general). Applied with Alice's observables negated it also gives -S <= 2, so for a unit product vector it implies all of this repository's abs_chsh_le_of_isProduct. It also exhibits the Bell state at the Tsirelson value. It does not state that every non-product pure state violates CHSH; that direction, and the equivalence, are what is new here.",
        "relationship": "independent"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://isa-afp.org/entries/TsirelsonBound.html",
        "note": "Isabelle/HOL, Archive of Formal Proofs: M. Echenim, M. Mhalla and C. Mori, \"The CHSH inequality: Tsirelson's upper-bound and other results\" (2023). Proves that separable density matrices cannot violate the CHSH bound, Tsirelson's bound, and that the Bell state attains it. Covers the product bound; does not state Gisin's theorem.",
        "relationship": "independent"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://isa-afp.org/entries/Projective_Measurements.html",
        "note": "Isabelle/HOL, Archive of Formal Proofs: M. Echenim, \"Quantum projective measurements and the CHSH inequality\" (2021). Projective measurements, the CHSH inequality and its quantum violation. Does not state Gisin's theorem.",
        "relationship": "independent"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/stalex444/pdt-lean/tree/0dae307fb786a3d180bba137a44555a1bf645637",
        "note": "Palomar PALOMAR-2026-08-19-000007. Operator-level CHSH results for Mathlib's IsCHSHTuple: the Landau identity, Tsirelson's bound in norm form, the classical constant under a commuting party. Not about states; does not state Gisin's theorem.",
        "relationship": "independent"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/stalex444/tsirelson-contractions/tree/ef7bd3b81c4cda7030329bc1057df7b00e9efb9b",
        "note": "Palomar PALOMAR-2026-10-28-000030. The same operator-level CHSH bounds for self-adjoint contractions, by dilation, with state corollaries bounding the CHSH value. Does not state Gisin's theorem.",
        "relationship": "independent"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/zblore/csd-lean4/blob/0b6012ce2c572ebc115675a3022fa3a90eb0beb7/CsdLean4/LF6/GisinTheorem.lean",
        "note": "The author's earlier two-qubit case inside the CSD project: for c|00> + s|11> with real c, s > 0, explicit Pauli settings give the CHSH value 2 sqrt(1 + 4c^2 s^2) (gisin_chsh_value, gisin_chsh_violation). Not imported here; the idea of tilting Bob's settings by the concurrence is reused in the two-dimensional step.",
        "relationship": "other"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/5e0c4e5239cb0a2d86d68a884bf52cfd963fce22/Mathlib/Algebra/Star/CHSH.lean",
        "note": "Mathlib's CHSH_inequality_of_comm and tsirelson_inequality, for CHSH tuples in an ordered star-ring. Abstract operator inequalities; they say nothing about states. Not used.",
        "relationship": "other"
      }
